# Keep the build context small and free of host state. Without this file every
# `docker build` sends the whole repository to the daemon, including server/.env
# (real GEMINI_API_KEY), the .git history, and the Flutter/Node build trees.
#
# Neither Dockerfile COPYs these today, but a future `COPY . .` would sweep
# server/.env into an image layer silently. Excluding them here makes that
# impossible rather than merely unlikely.

# Real secrets and local env.
.env
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Version control and tooling state.
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github

# Python build/runtime state.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.venv
**/venv
**/*.egg-info

# Node / web-ui build trees.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.vite
**/.turbo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Flutter / Dart build trees.
app/build
app/.dart_tool
app/.flutter-plugins
app/.flutter-plugins-dependencies
app/**/ephemeral
app/**/Pods

#
# Local runtime stores. Dot-prefixed on purpose: created under /data
# inside the container by server.Dockerfile, so no source tree is named
# like them.
#
# Deliberately NOT a bare data glob: that pattern matches any directory
# named `data` at any depth, including web-ui/src/data/ which is real SPA
# source. Excluding it breaks vite build on src/data/*.
**/.uploads
**/.cache
**/.shares
**/.submissions
**/.classes

# Docs, diagrams and scratch are not needed to build either image.
docs
tmp
research
*.md
!README.md

# OS noise.
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
